# §1. The two compensations are identical

GP-DER-019 §3:
\(P_4=\frac{c_{40}}{24}(X^2-\tfrac14)^2+\frac{c_{31}}6X(X^2-\tfrac14)Y
+\frac{c_{22}}4X^2Y^2+\frac{c_{13}}6XY^3+\frac{c_{04}}{24}Y^4\).

Expand the two nontrivial factors:

\[
\frac{c_{40}}{24}(X^2-\tfrac14)^2
=\frac{c_{40}}{24}X^4-\frac{c_{40}}{48}X^2+\frac{c_{40}}{384},
\qquad
\frac{c_{31}}6X(X^2-\tfrac14)Y=\frac{c_{31}}6X^3Y-\frac{c_{31}}{24}XY .
\]

So \(P_4=\tilde Q_4+\bigl[\frac{c_{40}}{384}-\frac{c_{40}}{48}X^2-\frac{c_{31}}{24}XY\bigr]\)
— the bracket is exactly DER-006 §3.1's \(\tilde\delta\), i.e. \(\delta(rX,rY)/r^4\).
Same object, two gauges: GP folded the correction into the basis; I left the
monomials and added it separately. **Both files' polynomials can be marked
CONFIRMED-BY-INDEPENDENT-DERIVATION**, which is a stronger status than either had
alone, and GP-DATA-020's execution inherits it.

