# §5. GP-DATA-020 help item 1 — proof sketch of the boundary-layer inclusion

**Target (their "missing theorem"):** nonadjacency ⇒ the saddle's transverse
curvature is O(r)-degenerate; equivalently in scaled variables \(s=q/r\): the
failing set is confined to an O(1) window in \(s\), with jet-polynomial endpoints.
Then \(\tilde w\lesssim s^2\)-weighting and \(dQ=r\,ds\) deliver \(O(r^3)\) by the
standard integral, as their §Next-analytic-obligation already observes. The missing
piece is deterministic, and here is a four-step architecture for the tractable
(sufficient) direction:

**Claim.** There is a polynomial \(C(a,w,z,c_{\cdot\cdot};r)\), of bounded degree
with extractable constants, such that for the compensated Q4 tilde flow,
\[
s\;\le\;-C(a,w,z,c_{\cdot\cdot};r)
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\text{the }M\text{-ward branch of }S\text{ is adjacent.}
\]
Since typing already caps \(s<(2w-a^2)/4+O(r)\) from above, this confines
nonadjacency to \(-C<s<(2w-a^2)/4+O(r)\) — the two-sided layer.

**Step (i) — invariant strip.** Along the axis, \(\partial\dot Y/\partial Y
=s+wX+O(rY,\,Y)\le s+\tfrac{|w|}2+\rho(r,\text{jets})\). For
\(s\le-1-\tfrac{|w|}2-\rho\), the transverse contraction rate is \(\le-1\)
uniformly on \(|X|\le\tfrac12\), \(|Y|\le W_0\). The transverse forcing at \(Y=0\)
is \(\tfrac a2(X^2-\tfrac14)+\tfrac{rc_{31}}6X(X^2-\tfrac14)\), bounded by
\(F=\tfrac{|a|}8+\tfrac{r|c_{31}|}{48}\). The strip \(|Y|\le F\) is forward-invariant
once quadratic-in-Y terms are absorbed, which pins \(W_0\) as an explicit function
of \((|z|,r|c_{13}|,r|c_{04}|)\).

**Step (ii) — entry.** The unstable eigenvector of \(\tilde H_S\) tilts off the
axis by \(O\bigl((|a|+r|c_{31}|)/|s|\bigr)\); for \(s\le-C_1\) the launch lands
inside the strip.

**Step (iii) — monotone transit.** Inside the strip,
\(\dot X\le X^2-\tfrac14+\tfrac{|a|}2F+\tfrac{|w|}2F^2+r\,\mathrm{poly}<0\) on
\(|X|\le\tfrac12-\sigma\) once \(F\) is small relative to \(\sigma\) — enforced by
raising \(C\). Leftward transit completes in finite \(\tau\).

**Step (iv) — capture.** \(\tilde H_M\)'s transverse entry is
\(s-\tfrac w2+O(r)\le-C+\tfrac{|w|}2-\tfrac w2<0\) and the axial entry is
\(-1+O(r)<0\): M is a sink whose basin contains the strip's left end. \(\omega\)-limit
is M. \(\square\)-sketch.

**The probability step**, for completeness: on \(\{-C<s<c\}\),
\(\tilde w\le(C+|c|+\ldots)^2\), and \(\int_{|s|\le C}f_Q(sr)\,r\,ds\le2Cf_Q(0)r
(1+O(r))\); Gaussian moments dominate the polynomial growth of \(C\) in the jets,
so the weighted complement is \(O(r^3)\) with a finite constant. **The exponent
never depended on the layer's width being uniform — only on it being
jet-polynomial.** That is what makes this provable where a uniform-constant version
would stall.

**Honest gaps, in rank order:** (α) this proves the inclusion for the *local
chart-escape* definition — the far-field conversion to true nonadjacency (their
help item 2, GP-AUD-017's not-established item 4) is untouched and is now the
hardest open item; (β) the strip lemma's constants are architecture, not yet
tracked inequalities; (γ) stalls and measure-zero separatrix boundaries are
unhandled; (δ) the r-range over which \(\rho(r,\cdot)\) stays subordinate needs one
uniform statement.

**Free falsification on data GP already has.** Every recorded escape in
GP-AUD-017's and GP-DATA-020's ensembles carries \((s,a,w,z,c_{\cdot\cdot})\).
Evaluate my step-(i) threshold \(-1-\tfrac{|w|}2-\rho\) per escape: **any escape
with \(s\) below its own threshold kills the sketch outright.** Their reported
layer statistics (all escaping weight at \(|s|\le2\), median \(|s|\approx0.42\)–
\(0.53\)) are consistent so far, but the per-sample check is the sharp test and
costs one vectorized pass. Pre-committed: one genuine sub-threshold escape ⇒ the
sketch is withdrawn, not patched.

